1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
WeType Quick: an unofficial Quick input patch for WeType.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
This is an illustrated introduction, not a phone screen recording.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Choose Quick (速成) in the original keyboard/input-method picker.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Switch back to an original input mode whenever needed.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Type enym continuously, corresponding to the roots 水弓卜一.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
The roots stay in the composition area; suggestions include 測試.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Select a suggestion to commit the text to the input field.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Quick connects to the original keys, suggestion strip, and expanded list.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
This diagram shows the structure; the actual appearance varies by settings and device.

10
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Compose words and phrases, up to 8 characters or 16 roots at a time.

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Quick learns selection ranking locally; long-press a suggestion to pin or remove it.

12
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
The upward clear gesture on Delete clears roots and text before the cursor.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Text after the cursor remains. This Quick clear action has no downward-swipe undo.

14
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,000
If Bluetooth is detected when voice input starts, the patch requests the phone's built-in mic.

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Devices may ignore that preference, and re-signing may affect offline speech recognition.

16
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
The added Quick engine runs locally. The original app's network behavior has not been fully audited.

17
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The project provides added source code and patch tools; obtain the supported original APK yourself.

18
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,000
See the project README for rebuild instructions, limitations, and licenses.

19
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
An unofficial project, not affiliated with or endorsed by Tencent.
